---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';

// Completed against the ICO's list of what a privacy notice must say:
// https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/uk-gdpr-guidance-and-resources/individual-rights/the-right-to-be-informed/what-privacy-information-should-we-provide/
// Facts that aren't settled yet are shown as visible [to confirm: …] placeholders.
const controller = site.company
  ? `${site.company.name}, registered in ${site.company.registeredIn}, company number ${site.company.number}, registered office ${site.company.office}`
  : null;
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy · ${site.name}`}
  description="No cookies, no tracking, and what happens to an email you send us."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="page wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="opening__lede">
      This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics or tracking, and loads nothing from anyone else. The only personal
      information we handle is what you send us by email.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {
        controller ? (
          <>{controller} is the controller of your personal information.</>
        ) : (
          <>{site.name} is the controller of your personal information. [to confirm: the company’s registered name, number and office, once it is incorporated]</>
        )
      }
      You can contact us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Visiting the site</h2>
    <p>
      Like any website, the service that hosts it handles your IP address and browser details to deliver the pages and keep
      the service secure. We don’t use them to identify you. Hosting: [to confirm: the hosting provider].
    </p>
    <p>
      If you pause the background animation, your browser remembers that choice in its own local storage, so it stays paused
      next time. It never leaves your device, and nothing is stored until you choose.
    </p>

    <h2>Emailing us</h2>
    <p>
      If you email us, we use your name, address and message to reply and to keep a record of the conversation. Our lawful
      basis is legitimate interests: answering your enquiry. We don’t add you to a mailing list, sell your details or share
      them with anyone except the services that carry and store our email: [to confirm: the email provider].
    </p>
    <p>We keep emails for [to confirm: the retention period], then delete them.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us for a copy of the information we hold about you, and ask us to correct it, delete it, restrict how we use
      it or stop using it. Email us and we’ll reply within a month.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you’re unhappy with how we handle your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office:
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a> or 0303 123 1113.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
